From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Date: Mon, 17 Aug 2026 20:00:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7996: skip recovery before registration

An MCU timeout during mt7996_init_hardware() schedules reset_work before
mt76_register_device() has initialized the mac80211 workqueue.  The reset
worker then calls ieee80211_restart_hw() against a partially registered hw,
causing a NULL pointer dereference instead of letting probe fail normally.

Do not start runtime firmware recovery until device registration has
completed.  The probe path already returns the MCU timeout and unwinds the
partially initialized device.

Signed-off-by: Codex <codex@openai.com>
---
 mt7996/mcu.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

--- a/mt7996/mcu.c
+++ b/mt7996/mcu.c
@@ -229,6 +229,9 @@ static int mt7996_mcu_parse_response(stru
 		dev_err(mdev->dev, "Message %08x (seq %d) timeout\n",
 			cmd, seq);
 
+		if (!dev->recovery.hw_init_done)
+			return -ETIMEDOUT;
+
 		if (!test_and_set_bit(MT76_MCU_RESET, &dev->mphy.state)) {
 			dev->recovery.restart = true;
 			wake_up(&dev->mt76.mcu.wait);
